      "content": "#include <iostream>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <cstdlib>\n#include <climits>\n#include <omp.h>\n\nint main() {\n    int n, s;\n    std::cin >> n >> s;\n\n    // Allocate aligned flat matrix (64-byte alignment for SIMD)\n    int* mat = nullptr;\n    if (posix_memalign((void**)&mat, 64, static_cast<size_t>(n) * n * sizeof(int)) != 0) {\n        return 1;\n    }\n\n    // Read input\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            scanf(\"%d\", &mat[i * n + j]);\n        }\n    }\n\n    const int np1 = n + 1;\n    // Allocate aligned prefix sum array\n    long long* pref = nullptr;\n    if (posix_memalign((void**)&pref, 64, static_cast<size_t>(np1) * np1 * sizeof(long long)) != 0) {\n        free(mat);\n        return 1;\n    }\n\n    // Initialize first row and column to zero\n    for (int j = 0; j < np1; ++j) pref[j] = 0LL;\n    for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) pref[i * np1] = 0LL;\n\n    // First pass: horizontal cumulative sums per row\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        long long row_sum = 0;\n        const int base_i = (i + 1) * np1;\n        const int mat_base = i * n;\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            row_sum += mat[mat_base + j];\n            pref[base_i + (j + 1)] = row_sum;\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Second pass: vertical accumulation\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        const int base_cur = (i + 1) * np1;\n        const int base_prev = i * np1;\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            pref[base_cur + (j + 1)] += pref[base_prev + (j + 1)];\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Search for maximum SxS submatrix sum using OpenMP parallel collapse(2)\n    int mxSum = INT_MIN;\n    const int limit = n - s;  // inclusive upper bound\n\n    #pragma omp parallel for collapse(2) reduction(max:mxSum)\n    for (int i = 0; i <= limit; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j <= limit; ++j) {\n            long long sum = pref[(i + s) * np1 + (j + s)]\n                          - pref[i * np1 + (j + s)]\n                          - pref[(i + s) * np1 + j]\n                          + pref[i * np1 + j];\n            if (sum > mxSum) mxSum = static_cast<int>(sum);\n        }\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", mxSum);\n\n    free(mat);\n    free(pref);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Integrating contiguous storage with aligned allocation (from B), two-pass integral image construction (from A), and OpenMP parallel collapse(2) reduction over all starting positions (from C) yields a correct and fast solution.",
